# Owner-only files are the ones that judge or gate a merge or a deploy (m14,
# branchLeft/workspace#2265; source list: branchLeft/workspace#2314). Every
# other path is merged on the reviewer App's approval, with no catch-all line.
# Gate files are listed by their existing path. The Ansible loader directories are the
# exception: they are listed before any file is in them, so a first file in one is already
# the owner's. Their names come from ansible-core, and ansible/checks/test_codeowners.py
# fails when a loader has no line. No pattern is matched by a word in a file name, so
# ordinary role work is not owner-gated by its name.
# A new gate file is added here by its path, in the pull request that adds it.

# Estate files the merge script refuses at gate 6: mail/ runs under plan credentials on push, and every credentialed plan job installs from the lockfiles, pnpm-workspace.yaml files (which hold allowBuilds) and .npmrc files below.
/mail/                                   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/pnpm-lock.yaml                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/pnpm-lock.yaml                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner-host/pnpm-lock.yaml             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/pnpm-workspace.yaml             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner-host/pnpm-workspace.yaml        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.npmrc                                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner/.npmrc                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/hetzner-host/.npmrc                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The review rule itself. GitHub reads this file from .github/ first; /.github/ at the foot of this file owns the workflows and actions as well.
